WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.434
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.634
You're here. You made it.
You're watching.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.868
Thank you for watching our show.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.567
Well, guys, tomorrow
is Thanksgiving.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.167
That's right.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.767
It's here.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.734
Thanksgiving -- it's the day
that you forget about

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:18.067
all the fighting and division
in the world

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:20.067
and just focus on all
the fighting and division

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:22.234
in your family.

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:24.601
That's right. Since it's
the night before Thanksgiving,

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:27.200
lots of Americans are getting
their antibodies checked

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.067
to see if they can fight off
Aunt Rita's mystery casserole.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.367
I'm actually hosting
Thanksgiving.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:34.634
My favorite part is guessing

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.200
which relative
is going to get the one chair

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.868
that's shorter
than all the others.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.067
"Can someone
please pass the...?"

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.801
[ Applause ]

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:46.667
Of course, lots of people
will be making turkey,

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:49.667
while others will be
cooking a turducken.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:52.501
You know what a turducken --
It's a coronary inside a stroke

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:53.834
inside a heart attack.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:56.901
I read that the night
before Thanksgiving

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:58.868
is one of the biggest
drinking nights of the year

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:01.734
because so many people
go to their home-town bars

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.868
to see old friends,
and I think the bars know this.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.767
I mean, just take a look
at some of the signs

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.767
I saw they put outside.
This one says...

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:13.567
-Wow.
-That's not -- Look at this one.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.801
Next up, there's...

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.067
And finally, there's...

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:34.334
There you go. That's --

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:35.834
I want to say hi
to all my friends

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:38.467
at the exchange right now.
Hi.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.834
Hey, did you guys see this?

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:42.467
Tom Brady said that Thanksgiving
is the one day of the year

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:46.234
where he says "screw it" and
eats just like everyone else.

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:47.501
Yeah, and apparently,

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.100
the meal really takes
a toll on Tom Brady.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.667
Here he is before Thanksgiving.

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.634
And here he is
after Thanksgiving.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:55.033
It's just...

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:56.901
You just got to be careful,
you know?

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.901
-A lot of inflammation.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:00.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:03.133
Some business news.
The CEO of Ocean Spray said

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:06.701
that due to a can shortage
from supply-chain issues,

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.100
people who want cranberry sauce

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.734
might have to use
fresh cranberries.

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:13.200
I'm pretty sure this is
the first supply-chain issue

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.200
where everyone thought, "Good."

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.667
Of course, Thanksgiving
isn't just about food.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:23.901
It's all about posting pictures
of your food on social media.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.667
But there's some important
things to know

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:27.501
about posting
your Thanksgiving plate.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.300
So I wrote a tiny song about it.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:41.901
♪♪

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:45.834
♪ PSA, Thanksgiving food
doesn't photograph too good ♪

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:49.534
♪ It just looks like
a big old pile of beige ♪

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.467
♪ I'm sure your dinner
tasted great ♪

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.334
♪ But that tan rainbow
on your plate's ♪

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:57.501
♪ Not showing up on no one's
"For You" page ♪

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.534
♪ Mystery scoops
of brown and white ♪

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:01.567
♪ Gravy filmed by candlelight ♪

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:05.534
♪ Ain't the look
that home cooking deserves ♪

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:08.767
♪ Hashtag dinner,
hashtag snacky ♪

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:11.167
♪ All looks like
you served wet khakis ♪

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:14.834
♪ Bowls of soggy burlap
for dessert ♪

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:18.868
♪ So, PSA, Thanksgiving food
doesn't photograph too good ♪

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:22.501
♪ In worst-case scenarios
looks gross ♪

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.901
♪ Just take a picture
with your fam ♪

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:27.501
♪ Or your friends together,
not of ham ♪

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:32.033
♪ That's why your mom told you
to wear nice clothes ♪

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:34.200
[ Song ends ]

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.501
Thank you. Thank you.

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:41.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:44.467
Thank you. Well, I --

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:46.901
I read that Russia is demanding
that, by next year,

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:49.300
large U.S. tech companies
like Facebook

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.033
opens up offices
in their country.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.801
Yep.
Facebook inside Russia.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.834
It's like a fake-news turducken.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.367 --> 00:03:59.234
Yep. Soon, Putin will be like,

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:04.400
"Oh, no, the spying is coming
from inside the house!"

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.767
This is cool, though.

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.467
Disney just announced
that next year

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.067
they're introducing
their very own

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:12.434
"Hey Disney" voice assistant
at Disneyland.

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:14.534
Well, not to be outdone,
another amusement park

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:16.100
is rolling out
something similar.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.367
Take a look at this.

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:20.033
-At Busch Gardens,
we're proud to introduce

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.400
our innovative
new voice assistant.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.601
Get all the information you need
by simply saying things like,

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:27.868
"Hey, Busch Gardens,
what's the weather?"

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.868
-[ Beep ]
-How the hell should I know?

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:31.334
-"Hey, Busch Gardens,

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:32.767
what should I bring
to the park?"

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:36.434
-Two flasks and a vape pan.
[ Coughing ]

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:39.267
-And, "Hey, Busch Gardens,
what should I do next?"

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:42.200
-[ Beep ]
-Try not to [bleep] die.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.801
-Busch Gardens.

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:46.167
Just like Disney.
If you drink enough.

00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:47.834
-Hey. That's nice.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:54.300
Some movie news.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.601
Today, "House of Gucci"
starring Lady Gaga

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.167
and Adam Driver
finally hit theaters.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yep.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.100
Tickets to "House of Gucci"
are $18,

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.701
but if you go to Times Square,
you can find a knockoff for $10.

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:07.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.367
"House of Bucci."

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:12.701
Get this. Actor Steve Burton
was fired from the soap opera

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:15.901
"General Hospital" 'cause
he refused to get vaccinated.

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:18.067
Yep, they kept showing him
evidence the vaccine was safe,

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.868
but he had amnesia.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:23.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:24.601
Yeah, wh--

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:26.801
-Wow.
-It's all right.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:29.033
When he found out he was fired,
Burton went up to the producer,

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.901
threw a drink in his face,
slapped him, and yelled,

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:33.033
"I'll always love you,"
then stormed out.

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:34.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.801
Hey, I heard
about a woman in Canada

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:42.434
who ordered a toy
for her granddaughter,

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:45.133
but it turned out
it wasn't very child-friendly.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:47.267
Look at this.
-Ania Tanner wanted to buy

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:49.400
an educational toy
for her granddaughter

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.434
and found this dancing cactus
on Walmart's website.

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:55.067
When it arrived, she decided
to listen to the songs,

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:57.601
one in English,
Spanish, and Polish.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:59.934
-It just happens
that I'm Polish.

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:02.667
And when I start listening to
the song and I heard the words,

00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:07.200
it's about taking five grams
of cocaine and being alone.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:14.133
-Her granddaughter was like --

00:06:14.133 --> 00:06:16.133
Her granddaughter was like,
"Yeah, I'm really disappointed

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:19.234
I won't get a Polish cactus
for Christmas."

00:06:19.234 --> 00:06:21.334
Has this woman
ever heard of a toy store?

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:23.100
Target? Go to Target.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.100
Can we see
that cactus toy again?

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.968
I think we could have guessed
he was on cocaine.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:31.868
Don't you think?

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:35.067
Finally, a truck carrying
$400,000 worth of Jack Daniel's

00:06:35.067 --> 00:06:36.667
overturned on
a Tennessee highway,

00:06:36.667 --> 00:06:38.300
spilled whiskey
all over the road.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.133
After it happened,
officials didn't know

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.033
whether to clean it up
or tip over a truck

00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:43.634
carrying Coca-Cola.

